-- Three cities that reached five active rows through owners whose own pages say American / NMJL (promotions in 0232): published with a written intro.
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'Tile & Table Tyrone, on Senoia Road, teaches American-style mahjong in Mahj 101 classes that run through the week, and also hosts guided play evenings and a lunch-and-play meetup at Chicken Salad Chick. It is a handy local option for the south side of Atlanta, where most groups meet closer to downtown. Classes are small and social, and supplies are on the table. Mahj 101 is the place to start if you have never played.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'tyrone';
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'In the Wyckoff area, Bams, Dots and Craks, Oh Mahj! runs beginner lessons that teach the tiles and how to read the National Mah Jongg League card, plus open play. Sessions rotate between a craft brewery in Wayne, the borough hall meeting room in Lincoln Park and Ridgewood Needlepoint in Wyckoff, so check the schedule for the right address. Start with the Mahjong 101 lesson if you are new to the game.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'wyckoff';
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'Slidell''s mahjong is Scramble Nights at The Painted Pagoda, a weekly evening of American mahjong run by Crescent & Tile Mahjong Co, with the occasional themed event such as a Halloween bash. The nights are for players who already know the rules, the Charleston and how to finish a game on their own, and no instruction is given at the table. If you are still learning, practice the basics with a friend first, then join a Scramble Night.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'slidell';
